ingle whistleblower indictment  and I think there is a war on  journalists and a broader war on  information going on in our country or  who's gonna win that were you hopeful  that kind of new media and new  technologies which on the one hand gives  the government more ways to surveil you  but on the other way also gives these  outlets for expression that you know  wouldn't have happened even ten years  ago I like to be optimistic and agreeing  with my client Edward Snowden that if  Congress doesn't take care of this that  tech will and you can see that I mean  Tech has gone ahead and created amazing  encryption devices and you could see the  government's frustration with that  because now in the UK and the US and  Australia they are trying to outlaw  encryption so you know I  and again the judicial branch I feel  like is finally turning on these issues  and ruling that secret surveillance is  unconstitutional and probably illegal so  I do see change going on in that branch  of government I'm hoping that ultimately  technology and Internet freedom will  prevail in this struggle well we'll  leave it there I hope you're right we've  been talking about jesselyn Radack she  is that exposed facts and she's a lawyer  to many whistleblowers and hopefully  more to come  jessalyn thanks for talking to us thank  you for reason TV I'm Nick Gillespie

